    {
      "_id": "vCnexktEBiykYP0v",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!PBJeE9T9n0BjB6ag.vCnexktEBiykYP0v",
      "name": "Mortal Days",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>Ezra worked six years for a big cloud company in South Lake Union. In 2018 he discovered that thousands of Seattle doorbell cameras were sending video to a server that didn&#39;t appear in any contract. He reported it internally. Two weeks later they fired him for a made-up “policy violation,” and no company in the city ever answered him again.</p>\n"
      },
      "sort": 200000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 2
      },
      "flags": {
        "seattle-by-night": {
          "origen": "pagina"
        }
      },
      "_stats": {
        "coreVersion": "14.365",
        "systemId": "wod5e",
        "systemVersion": "5.3.28"
      }
    },
    {
      "_id": "Unt6qGTgG6dtTmXb",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!PBJeE9T9n0BjB6ag.Unt6qGTgG6dtTmXb",
      "name": "Kindred Nights",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<p>Abel Thornquist (@UUID[JournalEntry.dj4gIszHHTN1QRKk]{Abel Thornquist}) Embraced him in 2019. He wanted someone who could see the city&#39;s digital nervous system the way he sees the tunnels. Ezra lives in the Sealed Underground (@UUID[JournalEntry.jg1zpvYlDFMJRY8Q]{The Sealed Underground (Seattle Underground)}), among recycled servers and cables that run down through 19th-century holes. He sells information with no face and no name. His Mask is an anonymous account on a dozen forums. He feeds on blood bags he gets by hacking a blood bank&#39;s inventory (<em>Bagger</em>).</p>\n"
      },
      "sort": 300000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 2
      },
      "flags": {
        "seattle-by-night": {
          "origen": "pagina"
        }
      },
      "_stats": {
        "coreVersion": "14.365",
